From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Clark <daniec@microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:25:21 -0700
Subject: Require left mouse button for renderer drags

In MouseEventManager::HandleMouseDraggedEvent the render process only
initiates drags when the left mouse button is held down. The
corresponding browser-process check in
WebContentsViewAura::StartDragging allows the drag to proceed if any
mouse button is held down. This could allow a compromised renderer to
cause drags to be triggered from mouse interactions that would not
normally initiate a drag.

Fix this mismatch by tightening the browser-process check to require the
left mouse button.

Fixed: 553150372
Change-Id: I01da0d2e5d7dff53f5b6cd6bf92b0c7217c868db
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8404057
Reviewed-by: Mitsuru Oshima <oshima@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Alex Moshchuk <alexmos@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Dan Clark <daniec@microsoft.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705348}

diff --git a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc
index 5e0fa708643b113449dd6b75975fb6147d944022..29d06081f76d35645ef93d4bd8bcfc28eae912ff 100644
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc
@@ -1265,14 +1265,14 @@ void WebContentsViewAura::StartDragging(
     // touch event would reach `::SendInput` via
     // DesktopWindowTreeHostWin::StartTouchDrag and could redirect the
     // synthesized click to an overlapping HWND (e.g. a permission bubble).
-    // Require an in-flight touch or mouse button, depending on the event
-    // source, and refuse the drag if requirement is not met.
+    // Require an in-flight touch or a left mouse button, depending on the
+    // event source, and refuse the drag if the requirement is not met.
     gfx::Point trusted_location = event_info.location;
     aura::Env* env = aura::Env::GetInstance();
     if ((event_info.source == ui::mojom::DragEventSource::kTouch &&
          !env->is_touch_down()) ||
         (event_info.source == ui::mojom::DragEventSource::kMouse &&
-         !env->IsMouseButtonDown())) {
+         !env->IsLeftMouseButtonDown())) {
       EndDrag(std::move(source_rwh_weak_ptr), result_op);
       return;
     }
